From ee3c5d2cb778ec875afeae7f2070fcf5a58f6a81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: don't re-apply selectFromDb to query-built views; map
 planetscale relational JSON (#1083, #554)

Follow-up to the selectFromDb hook for custom types:

- Columns of views defined with a query builder (`pgView(...).as(qb => ...)`,
  materialized views, mysql and sqlite views) are the output of a query that
  already applied the column's `selectFromDb` mapper. Selecting from such a
  view wrapped the value a second time (e.g. ST_AsText(ST_AsText(geo))).
  The view selection proxy now marks those columns as selection fields, so
  their mapper is not applied again. Views declared with raw SQL and explicit
  columns still apply the mapper, since they return the raw database value.
- MySQL relational queries in PlanetScale mode (built without lateral joins)
  now apply `selectFromDb` inside nested `json_array(...)` payloads, like the
  default mode already does.
- Regression tests for both cases.
